# UPGRADE-17
# Local AI Production Runtime
#
# Production-grade daemon supervision, multi-model hot/warm/cold pool,
# capacity-aware scheduling, adaptive load/unload, runtime recovery,
# measured routing, continuous performance regression,
# per-project inference profiles and zero-paid autonomous execution.
#
# PRIMARY PRINCIPLES:
#
# NO-COST FIRST
# LOCAL-FIRST
# CPU-FIRST MUST REMAIN SUPPORTED
# NO SILENT MODEL DOWNLOAD
# NO SILENT PAID FALLBACK
# NO FABRICATED PERFORMANCE DATA
# NO CLOUD DEPENDENCY FOR CORE OPERATION

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-16.

================================================================
MISSION
================================================================

Upgrade-14 through Upgrade-16 built:

- local provider abstraction
- model factory
- model registry
- llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM adapters
- hardware profiling
- model-fit estimation
- benchmark infrastructure
- local RAG
- MCP
- LocalAgentRuntime
- zero-paid-call enforcement
- auto-tuning architecture
- performance evidence framework

Upgrade-17 turns these components into a long-running, reliable,
resource-aware local inference service.

Target:

                    ZCoder Jobs
                         │
                         ▼
                Inference Scheduler
                         │
             ┌───────────┼────────────┐
             ▼           ▼            ▼
          Queue A      Queue B      Queue C
             │           │            │
             └───────────┼────────────┘
                         ▼
                Local Runtime Manager
                         │
       ┌─────────────────┼──────────────────┐
       ▼                 ▼                  ▼
   llama.cpp          Ollama              vLLM
       │                 │                  │
       └─────────────────┼──────────────────┘
                         ▼
                  Model Pool Manager
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼───────────────┐
          ▼              ▼               ▼
         HOT            WARM            COLD
          │
          ▼
   Hardware / RAM / VRAM
   Capacity Controller
          │
          ▼
   Continuous Measurement
          │
          ▼
   Benchmark-Aware Router

A developer should be able to leave ZCoder running locally for long
periods and have it:

- load the right model
- avoid OOM
- reuse warm models
- unload idle models
- recover crashed runtimes
- queue excess requests
- prevent paid fallback
- monitor actual performance
- select models using real evidence
- execute autonomous coding jobs
- remain useful on CPU-only hosts

================================================================
PHASE 0 — VERIFY UPGRADE-16
================================================================

Run:

git status --short
git log -30 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -30

python -m pytest -q -ra
python main.py --version
python -m build
git diff --check

Run the current release gate.

Inspect:

local_ai_stack.py
no_cost_platform.py
agent_runtime.py
release_gate.py
performance/benchmark code
model registry
runtime adapters
Web/API routes
tests/

Produce:

UPGRADE-16 EVIDENCE MATRIX

Capability
Claim
Evidence Level
Actual Artifact/Test
Real Runtime?
Verdict

Do not infer E4 from a passing unit suite.

================================================================
1. E4 CARRY-FORWARD RULE
================================================================

Only retain:

LOCAL_RUNTIME_VERIFIED = PASS E4

if Upgrade-16 contains reproducible evidence of:

- actual runtime process
- actual model artifact
- actual digest
- actual generated tokens
- actual timings
- zero prohibited provider calls

Only retain:

LOCAL_CODING_VERIFIED = PASS E4

if a real model:

- inspected code
- produced a patch
- ran validation
- fixed deterministic repository tests

Otherwise downgrade to the strongest proven tier.

================================================================
2. LOCAL RUNTIME MANAGER
================================================================

Create/consolidate:

LocalRuntimeManager

Responsibilities:

discover runtimes
start ZCoder-owned runtimes
observe external runtimes
health-check
load models
unload models
restart crashed managed runtimes
stop managed runtimes
report capacity

Do not mix job orchestration logic into this class.

================================================================
3. RUNTIME OWNERSHIP
================================================================

Runtime instances must be classified:

ZCODER_MANAGED
EXTERNAL

For ZCODER_MANAGED:

ZCoder may start/stop/restart it.

For EXTERNAL:

ZCoder may health-check and route to it.

ZCoder must never kill an external process merely because the endpoint
became unhealthy.

================================================================
4. RUNTIME INSTANCE MODEL
================================================================

Persist runtime state such as:

runtime_instance_id
runtime_type
owner
endpoint
pid
process_fingerprint
version
started_at
last_health_at
state
loaded_models
capacity
configuration_hash

================================================================
5. RUNTIME STATES
================================================================

Use explicit states:

STARTING
READY
BUSY
DEGRADED
DRAINING
STOPPING
STOPPED
FAILED

Do not encode state only through process existence.

================================================================
6. HEALTH MODEL
================================================================

Separate:

PROCESS_ALIVE
SERVER_READY
MODEL_READY
CAPACITY_AVAILABLE

A process can exist while model loading is incomplete.

================================================================
7. HEALTH CHECK ADAPTER
================================================================

Each runtime adapter determines its own documented health semantics.

Do not assume all local servers implement the same endpoint.

================================================================
8. MODEL RESIDENCY MODEL
================================================================

Create explicit states:

COLD
LOADING
WARM
HOT
EVICTING
UNLOADED
FAILED

Definitions must be documented.

Example:

COLD:
artifact exists but not resident.

WARM:
model resident but currently idle.

HOT:
resident and actively serving/recently used.

================================================================
9. MODEL POOL MANAGER
================================================================

Create:

ModelPoolManager

Responsibilities:

resident models
memory allocation
capacity
load
reuse
unload
eviction
preload

================================================================
10. NO DUPLICATE MODEL COPIES
================================================================

Do not launch multiple copies of the same large model unless:

measured concurrency requires it
and
hardware can safely support it.

Prefer shared runtime capacity first.

================================================================
11. MODEL SERVER KEY
================================================================

Server compatibility identity includes:

runtime
runtime version
model digest
tuning profile
context configuration
security scope

Do not reuse incompatible server instance.

================================================================
12. MEMORY ACCOUNTING
================================================================

Track:

host RAM total
host RAM available
runtime RSS
model estimated RAM
model measured RAM
GPU VRAM when available
KV/cache estimates
safety reserve

================================================================
13. ADMISSION CONTROL
================================================================

Before loading model or admitting job:

requirements
+
current resident models
+
available RAM/VRAM
+
runtime capacity
+
job priority

→ ADMIT
  QUEUE
  EVICT_THEN_ADMIT
  REJECT

================================================================
14. NEVER OOM DELIBERATELY
================================================================

Maintain configurable minimum memory headroom.

Do not start another server/model when predicted usage violates safety
policy.

================================================================
15. MEMORY PRESSURE MONITOR
================================================================

Continuously but cheaply observe host memory.

States:

NORMAL
PRESSURE
CRITICAL

Avoid high-frequency polling.

================================================================
16. MEMORY PRESSURE ACTION
================================================================

NORMAL:
normal scheduling

PRESSURE:
avoid new model loads

CRITICAL:
unload safe idle model / pause new jobs

Never terminate active job blindly unless necessary for host safety.

================================================================
17. EVICTION POLICY
================================================================

Support an evidence-driven policy such as:

idle first
least recently used
largest idle memory reclaim
project priority

Do not implement arbitrary eviction order.

================================================================
18. PINNED MODELS
================================================================

Allow operator/project configuration:

pin model

Pinned model should remain resident where safe.

Host-safety policy still overrides pinning.

================================================================
19. IDLE TTL
================================================================

Support model idle timeout.

Do not hardcode one global duration.

Possible levels:

runtime default
organization/project
model profile

================================================================
20. PRELOAD
================================================================

Support controlled preload for frequently used models.

Preload is optional.

Never preload every catalog model.

================================================================
21. PRELOAD SAFETY
================================================================

Preload only when:

artifact verified
fit safe
runtime healthy
cost policy compliant

================================================================
22. LLAMA.CPP ROUTER MODE
================================================================

Re-read CURRENT official llama.cpp server documentation.

If current router mode is stable enough for the target functionality,
integrate behind the llama.cpp adapter.

Potential responsibilities:

multiple model discovery
load
unload
autoload policy
max loaded models
health
slot state

Do not expose llama.cpp router-specific concepts to domain callers.

================================================================
23. LLAMA.CPP MODEL LIMIT
================================================================

Map ZCoder pool limits into runtime-supported model concurrency only
when the current runtime documents the required feature.

Otherwise retain ZCoder-side process pool management.

================================================================
24. OLLAMA RESIDENCY
================================================================

Re-read current official Ollama API.

Use documented model residency/load/unload controls.

Keep runtime-specific semantics inside Ollama adapter.

================================================================
25. OLLAMA PROCESS OBSERVATION
================================================================

Use documented running-model information where available to reconcile:

resident models
memory
context
expiry

Do not infer loaded model solely from recent ZCoder request history.

================================================================
26. VLLM RESIDENCY
================================================================

Re-read current official vLLM APIs.

Use documented health/load/metrics/sleep functionality only when
supported by active platform/runtime configuration.

Do not invoke development-only dangerous endpoints in normal production
mode.

================================================================
27. VLLM DEVELOPMENT ENDPOINTS
================================================================

Any endpoint explicitly documented as development-only must be disabled
or policy-gated in production profiles.

================================================================
28. INFERENCE SCHEDULER
================================================================

Create:

LocalInferenceScheduler

It schedules inference capacity, not engineering jobs themselves.

Input:

job_id
project
task
model requirement
runtime requirement
priority
context requirement
tool requirement
deadline optional

================================================================
29. CAPACITY SLOT
================================================================

Represent:

InferenceSlot

Fields:

runtime
model
server
capacity
active_requests
queue_depth
memory
health

================================================================
30. PER-MODEL QUEUE
================================================================

Requests for an already-loaded model should normally queue against that
capacity rather than spawning another model server immediately.

================================================================
31. GLOBAL QUEUE
================================================================

If no compatible resident model exists:

global router chooses:

reuse
load
evict/load
queue
reject

================================================================
32. QUEUE PRIORITY
================================================================

Use bounded priority classes.

Example:

INTERACTIVE
NORMAL
BACKGROUND

Do not allow permanent starvation.

================================================================
33. FAIRNESS
================================================================

Prevent one project/job from monopolizing all local inference capacity.

Use simple fair scheduling.

================================================================
34. CANCELLATION
================================================================

Queued inference:

cancel immediately.

Running inference:

propagate cancellation when runtime supports it.

Always clean local bookkeeping.

================================================================
35. TIMEOUT
================================================================

Support:

queue timeout
load timeout
inference timeout

Do not use one timeout for all phases.

================================================================
36. BACKPRESSURE
================================================================

Bound:

queued inference requests
model load requests
benchmark jobs

Reject clearly when limit exceeded.

Do not allow unlimited RAM-backed queues.

================================================================
37. RUNTIME CRASH DETECTION
================================================================

Detect:

process exit
health failure
connection failure
repeated malformed response

Distinguish transient vs terminal.

================================================================
38. CRASH RECOVERY
================================================================

ZCODER_MANAGED runtime:

bounded restart.

EXTERNAL runtime:

mark unavailable.

Do not restart endlessly.

================================================================
39. RESTART BUDGET
================================================================

Track:

restart_count
restart_window
last_failure

Exceeding threshold:

FAILED

and require cooldown/operator action.

================================================================
40. MODEL LOAD FAILURE
================================================================

Classify:

OOM
INVALID_MODEL
UNSUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURE
BAD_CONFIGURATION
CORRUPT_ARTIFACT
PROCESS_FAILURE
TIMEOUT

Do not flatten to RuntimeError.

================================================================
41. RECONCILIATION
================================================================

At ZCoder restart:

discover managed runtime records
inspect actual processes/endpoints
reconcile model residency
clear stale capacity claims
resume scheduler

================================================================
42. ORPHAN PROCESS SAFETY
================================================================

Before terminating a recorded PID:

verify process fingerprint.

PID reuse must never kill unrelated application.

================================================================
43. CAPACITY RECONCILIATION
================================================================

After runtime restart/crash:

reset or reconstruct inference slots.

No permanently BUSY phantom slot.

================================================================
44. REQUEST IDENTIFIERS
================================================================

Every local inference request receives:

inference_request_id

Link to:

job
attempt
runtime
model
project

================================================================
45. STREAMING ROUTER
================================================================

Streaming must preserve:

request identity
cancellation
terminal event
error state

Router must not buffer entire output unnecessarily.

================================================================
46. CONTEXT ISOLATION
================================================================

No prompt/conversation state may leak between:

jobs
projects
organizations

even if model weights/server are shared.

================================================================
47. PROMPT CACHE SECURITY
================================================================

If runtime prompt/KV caching is enabled:

verify cache behavior does not expose one tenant's content to another.

Add explicit isolation tests.

================================================================
48. CACHE POLICY
================================================================

Allow:

DISABLED
SAME_JOB
SAME_PROJECT_SAFE
RUNTIME_DEFAULT

Default to conservative behavior.

Do not enable cross-tenant prompt reuse.

================================================================
49. TOOL CONTEXT ISOLATION
================================================================

Shared model runtime never shares:

tool results
MCP credentials
workspace path
memory

between jobs.

================================================================
50. CONTINUOUS PERFORMANCE MONITOR
================================================================

Use real inference measurements generated during normal execution.

Collect bounded:

TTFT
prompt throughput
decode throughput
total latency
failure
memory

Do not turn every user request into a heavy benchmark.

================================================================
51. OBSERVED PERFORMANCE
================================================================

Separate:

BENCHMARK

from:

OBSERVED_PRODUCTION_LOCAL

Measurements from normal job execution use a distinct evidence source.

================================================================
52. PERFORMANCE EWMA
================================================================

Maintain lightweight rolling statistics.

Do not store unlimited raw timing samples.

Persist appropriate aggregates plus bounded recent observations.

================================================================
53. PERFORMANCE DRIFT
================================================================

Detect meaningful degradation:

TTFT
decode throughput
failure rate
OOM frequency

Thresholds configurable.

================================================================
54. QUALITY DRIFT
================================================================

Performance alone is insufficient.

Run deterministic quality regression fixtures periodically or after:

model digest change
runtime upgrade
tuning change

================================================================
55. ROUTER USES QUALITY
================================================================

A faster model with failing coding validation must not automatically
become default.

================================================================
56. ROUTING SCORE
================================================================

Routing combines:

capability
quality
latency
memory
availability
cost policy
residency
project evidence

Do not use opaque model prestige.

================================================================
57. ROUTING SOURCE QUALITY
================================================================

Preference order:

same-project measured evidence
same-host measured evidence
same-host benchmark
contract capability
catalog estimate

================================================================
58. CONFIDENCE
================================================================

Return:

HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

with explanation.

================================================================
59. ADAPTIVE ROUTING
================================================================

When preferred model becomes:

unhealthy
memory unsafe
quality regressed

choose next eligible zero-cost candidate.

Do not jump to paid provider.

================================================================
60. PAID FALLBACK FIREWALL
================================================================

Keep a central paid-provider firewall.

No component can bypass it:

scheduler
router
agent
workflow
MCP
recovery
fallback

================================================================
61. ZERO PAID POLICY
================================================================

When active:

PAID_PLATFORM
UNKNOWN

are forbidden.

CUSTOMER_KEY also forbidden unless explicitly allowed by separate
policy.

================================================================
62. TRANSPORT AUDIT
================================================================

Maintain prohibited-call counters for each autonomous job.

Persist result.

================================================================
63. STRICT LOCAL MODE
================================================================

For strict offline execution:

allow only:

loopback
local IPC
filesystem
approved local subprocess

================================================================
64. ONLINE ACQUISITION SEPARATION
================================================================

Model download belongs to:

ONLINE_ACQUISITION

not inference.

Once acquired, strict local execution can operate offline.

================================================================
65. SCHEDULER + MODEL DOWNLOAD
================================================================

Inference scheduler must never silently download a missing model.

Return:

MODEL_NOT_INSTALLED

plus recommendation.

================================================================
66. PROJECT MODEL PROFILE
================================================================

Persist per-project:

coding model preference
review model preference
embedding profile
runtime preference
cost policy
latency preference
quality floor

================================================================
67. AUTO PROFILE
================================================================

`auto` resolves from evidence.

Never mutate configured explicit model choice silently.

================================================================
68. PROFILE FALLBACK
================================================================

Explicit model unavailable:

policy determines:

queue
allow compatible local fallback
fail

================================================================
69. LOCAL AGENT INTEGRATION
================================================================

LocalAgentRuntime obtains inference through LocalInferenceScheduler.

Do not directly instantiate provider clients everywhere.

================================================================
70. WORKFLOW INTEGRATION
================================================================

Workflow agents use capability requirements.

Scheduler handles actual model allocation.

================================================================
71. RAG INTEGRATION
================================================================

Repository retrieval remains local.

Routing should consider:

RAG availability
context requirements
model context capacity

================================================================
72. MCP INTEGRATION
================================================================

Tool-capable jobs require appropriate model/runtime strategy.

MCP remains policy controlled.

================================================================
73. MULTI-MODEL WORKFLOW
================================================================

Allow different local models for:

planning
coding
review
embedding

only when evidence justifies it.

Avoid unnecessary model swapping on RAM-constrained hosts.

================================================================
74. SWAP COST
================================================================

Router considers model load/unload cost.

A marginally better cold model may be worse than a good hot model for
interactive task.

================================================================
75. WARMTH FACTOR
================================================================

Routing may account for:

HOT
WARM
COLD

as an optimization, after correctness/security constraints.

================================================================
76. CPU-ONLY OPTIMIZATION
================================================================

CPU-only remains first-class.

Optimize for:

bounded thread use
low parallelism where appropriate
resident small models
minimal swap/thrash

================================================================
77. GPU FUTURE
================================================================

GPU capacity abstraction remains compatible with:

NVIDIA
AMD
Apple

Do not claim verified GPU behavior without hardware.

================================================================
78. MODEL POOL STRESS TEST
================================================================

Using Fake/controlled runtimes:

simulate many jobs.

Verify:

pool limit
queue
eviction
fairness
no duplicate server
no OOM admission

================================================================
79. REAL LOCAL CONCURRENCY TEST
================================================================

If actual runtime exists:

run small bounded concurrent requests.

Measure:

latency
throughput
queueing
memory

Do not overload host.

================================================================
80. LOAD SHEDDING
================================================================

When system cannot safely accept more inference:

return explicit capacity status.

Do not crash host.

================================================================
81. ADAPTIVE IDLE TIMEOUT
================================================================

Optional:

models used frequently remain resident longer.

Rare large models unload earlier.

Algorithm should be understandable and bounded.

================================================================
82. MODEL USAGE STATISTICS
================================================================

Persist privacy-safe statistics:

load_count
request_count
last_used
failures
average resident duration

No prompt content needed.

================================================================
83. DAEMON SUPERVISOR
================================================================

Create:

LocalAIDaemonSupervisor

for ZCoder-owned processes.

Responsibilities:

startup
shutdown
signal handling
health
restart
drain
process cleanup

================================================================
84. GRACEFUL ZCODER SHUTDOWN
================================================================

On shutdown:

stop accepting inference
drain/finish according to policy
persist state
terminate ZCoder-owned model servers cleanly

External servers remain untouched.

================================================================
85. SYSTEM BOOT
================================================================

Do not automatically load large models merely because ZCoder starts.

Default:

lazy load

unless explicit preload policy exists.

================================================================
86. SERVICE MODE
================================================================

Support long-running local daemon/service mode.

Example conceptual command:

zcoder local-ai serve

Follow current CLI conventions.

================================================================
87. STATUS
================================================================

Provide:

zcoder local-ai status

Show:

runtime
model pool
resident models
queues
capacity
RAM
health
zero-paid policy

================================================================
88. MODEL POOL CLI
================================================================

Potential commands:

zcoder local-ai models
zcoder local-ai load MODEL
zcoder local-ai unload MODEL
zcoder local-ai drain

Require appropriate local/operator authorization.

================================================================
89. SCHEDULER CLI
================================================================

Provide diagnostic:

zcoder local-ai queue

No hidden scheduling state.

================================================================
90. ROUTING EXPLAIN CLI
================================================================

Provide:

zcoder models explain --task coding --project ...

Include:

selected
evidence
warm state
quality
performance
memory
policy

================================================================
91. WEB LOCAL AI OPERATIONS
================================================================

If SELF_HOSTED Web profile is supported, add service-backed UI:

Runtime
Model Pool
Queues
Memory
Health
Performance
Routing
Regressions

No mock cards.

================================================================
92. LIVE UPDATE
================================================================

Use existing realtime infrastructure.

Durable state remains source of truth.

================================================================
93. PERFORMANCE CHART
================================================================

Show actual measured history.

Label:

BENCHMARK
OBSERVED
SIMULATED

clearly.

================================================================
94. MEMORY CHART
================================================================

Show:

available RAM
resident model footprint
runtime RSS
safety reserve

Do not fabricate GPU telemetry on CPU host.

================================================================
95. ALERTS
================================================================

Local in-app notifications:

runtime crash
repeated restart
memory pressure
model OOM
performance regression
quality regression

No paid alert provider required.

================================================================
96. SELF-HEALING LIMIT
================================================================

Self-healing must be bounded.

No infinite runtime restart loop.

================================================================
97. MODEL QUARANTINE
================================================================

Repeatedly crashing/corrupt model can become:

QUARANTINED

until operator revalidates/removes it.

================================================================
98. PROFILE QUARANTINE
================================================================

A tuning profile causing repeated OOM/crash should be disabled.

Fall back to last known safe profile.

================================================================
99. LAST KNOWN GOOD
================================================================

Persist:

last_known_good_runtime_profile
last_known_good_model_selection

Use only if still compatible with:

digest
runtime
hardware
policy

================================================================
100. CANARY TUNING
================================================================

New tuning profile should be tested with bounded workload before making
it default.

================================================================
101. CONTINUOUS BENCHMARKING
================================================================

Do not constantly benchmark.

Trigger on:

new model
new runtime
changed hardware
manual request
scheduled low-frequency maintenance

================================================================
102. IDLE BENCHMARK
================================================================

Optional benchmark only when host is sufficiently idle.

Do not compete with active developer job.

================================================================
103. PERFORMANCE REGRESSION GATE
================================================================

Release/runtime update may compare against stored baseline.

Do not fail release from noisy 1% variation.

Use meaningful thresholds.

================================================================
104. QUALITY REGRESSION GATE
================================================================

Coding/tool correctness regressions take priority over minor speedups.

================================================================
105. MODEL UPGRADE POLICY
================================================================

A new digest/tag is never silently promoted solely because "latest".

Acquire → verify → benchmark → canary → promote.

================================================================
106. MODEL PROMOTION
================================================================

States may include:

CANDIDATE
VALIDATED
PREFERRED
QUARANTINED
RETIRED

Separate from artifact download state.

================================================================
107. RUNTIME UPGRADE POLICY
================================================================

Same pattern:

detect new runtime
verify compatibility
benchmark
compare
promote

Do not auto-install runtime upgrades in core execution.

================================================================
108. LOCAL PRODUCTION DATA
================================================================

Performance/model pool state belongs in persistent local DB or current
storage abstraction.

Do not require Redis.

================================================================
109. SQLITE MODE
================================================================

Single-host local runtime must work with SQLite.

================================================================
110. POSTGRESQL SELF-HOSTED MODE
================================================================

Multi-process/self-hosted deployments may use PostgreSQL.

Do not introduce separate queue infrastructure.

================================================================
111. PROCESS LOCKING
================================================================

Prevent two ZCoder supervisors on same host from managing the same
runtime process accidentally.

Use safe OS/storage coordination.

Do not rely solely on in-memory mutex.

================================================================
112. PORT COLLISION
================================================================

Dynamic port allocation must be race-safe where multiple processes may
operate.

================================================================
113. SECURITY
================================================================

Audit:

runtime ownership
loopback binding
process command injection
model path traversal
model digest
runtime endpoint SSRF
prompt cache tenant isolation
queue tenant isolation
MCP
RAG
paid-provider firewall
logs

================================================================
114. COMMAND INJECTION
================================================================

Runtime process arguments must use structured argv.

Never build shell command from arbitrary model/project input.

================================================================
115. MODEL PATH
================================================================

Only verified registered artifacts may be passed into managed runtime.

No arbitrary user-controlled path escape.

================================================================
116. LOCAL SERVER AUTH BOUNDARY
================================================================

Loopback server may have different authentication semantics from remote
server.

Never treat remote/LAN endpoint as trusted simply because runtime type is
"local".

================================================================
117. REMOTE LOCAL-RUNTIME CONFIG
================================================================

If endpoint is not loopback:

classify it separately.

Apply:

authentication
TLS
SSRF
network policy

as applicable.

================================================================
118. FAULT INJECTION TESTS
================================================================

Test:

runtime crash
model load OOM
health timeout
queue overflow
memory pressure
stale runtime PID
port collision
corrupt model
bad tuning profile

================================================================
119. TENANT ISOLATION TESTS
================================================================

Two organizations sharing model weights:

no prompt leakage
no cache leakage
no job state leakage
no tool credential leakage

================================================================
120. QUEUE FAIRNESS TEST
================================================================

Tenant/project A floods scheduler.

B still receives bounded fair service.

================================================================
121. RESTART RECOVERY TEST
================================================================

Start managed model runtime.

Persist state.

Kill/restart ZCoder.

Reconcile accurately.

Do not duplicate runtime process.

================================================================
122. MODEL EVICTION TEST
================================================================

Simulate constrained memory.

Load A.
Request B.

Verify intended eviction/queue behavior.

================================================================
123. ACTIVE MODEL PROTECTION
================================================================

Never evict model serving an active request.

================================================================
124. EXTERNAL RUNTIME PROTECTION
================================================================

Never unload/stop model on external runtime unless adapter/policy
explicitly permits management.

================================================================
125. OFFLINE E2E
================================================================

With already-installed local artifact:

network denied
→ runtime start
→ model load
→ coding job
→ RAG
→ tools
→ validation
→ result

Prove prohibited outbound transport calls = 0.

================================================================
126. CPU PRODUCTION E2E
================================================================

On CPU-only environment:

run bounded system scenario.

Report real resource/performance evidence if real model is available.

================================================================
127. REAL RUNTIME EVIDENCE
================================================================

If actual model/runtime available:

record separately:

runtime
version
model
digest
resident state
load time
TTFT
prompt tok/s
decode tok/s
RSS
concurrent requests
failure rate

================================================================
128. REAL CODING EVIDENCE
================================================================

Do not reuse fake autonomous repair as real proof.

Use actual model if claiming E4.

================================================================
129. RELEASE PROFILES
================================================================

Maintain:

CORE_FREE
SELF_HOSTED
LOCAL_RUNTIME_VERIFIED
LOCAL_CODING_VERIFIED
PERFORMANCE_VERIFIED

Add:

LOCAL_PRODUCTION_RUNTIME

================================================================
130. LOCAL_PRODUCTION_RUNTIME PROFILE
================================================================

Requires at minimum:

runtime supervisor
model pool
admission control
queue
memory safety
crash recovery
bounded self-healing
routing
zero-paid firewall
offline execution
tenant/job isolation

Real local model E4 remains separately reported.

================================================================
131. NO-COST RELEASE RULE
================================================================

No cloud/paid credential may be required to pass:

CORE_FREE
LOCAL_PRODUCTION_RUNTIME

================================================================
132. WEB RELEASE EVIDENCE
================================================================

If self-hosted Web is part of profile:

install Web dependencies
run Web tests

Do not leave Web skipped while claiming strong Web evidence.

================================================================
133. TEST ACCOUNTING
================================================================

Report separately:

unit
scheduler
pool
supervisor
failure injection
security
