## 30. Remaining Limitations

Explicitly state:

actual model-generated tokens?
real llama.cpp?
real Ollama?
real vLLM?
real autonomous repair?
measured concurrency?
CPU only?
NVIDIA?
AMD?
Apple?
PITR?
PostgreSQL HA?
multi-region?

## 31. Final Verdict

Never use a passing unit suite as evidence of an actual model runtime.

Never report an external runtime as ZCoder-managed.

Never report model residency from stale local state.

Never continue loading models when memory admission says unsafe.

Never silently route to a paid provider.

Never call the platform "production local AI verified" if runtime
supervision, memory admission, recovery and isolation have not actually
been exercised.

Upgrade-17 succeeds when the local AI layer behaves like a reliable
long-running inference service rather than a collection of model
adapter classes.